"On the first run for a model shape this takes a few minutes: tools/baro reads the architecture and dimensions from the GGUF header, compiles an engine for exactly that shape, and converts the weights into a pack. Both go to ~/.cache/baro/<shape-id>/ (override with $BARO_CACHE). Every later run of the same file starts in seconds, and another checkpoint of the same shape reuses the compiled engine. An unsupported architecture or tokenizer is refused before any build starts."
