"1. **Environment variables** read by the engine (BARO_*). The Rust front passes its own environment to the engine and adds --engine-env KEY=VALUE. 2. **Profiles** in profiles/*.toml: a named set of settings for one use, such as turbo27b-coder.toml (27B as a 131k-context coding server). tools/baro serve --profile NAME. 3. **Build flags** (-D NAME=VALUE), which fix the model shape and some kernel choices at compile time. tools/baro sets these from the GGUF. Every setting the code reads is listed, with its type, default, range, restart need and a help text, in [docs/settings.toml](docs/settings.toml), the single source the face reads. tools/settings-check.mojo fails if that file and the source disagree, and generates the table below. The ones you are most likely to touch: Status, honestly: it is **correct and slow**. Teacher-forced against the GPU build, 1280 of 1280 ids agree (20 prompts x 64 ids, bench/check-cpu-engine.sh, GPU side built with -D BARO_SHARED_EXP=1 and BARO_MEGA=0). Decode"
